<title>UK: Treasuries closed in London, U.S. Independence Day.</title>
<headline>Treasuries closed in London, U.S. Independence Day.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Treasuries market was closed in London on Friday with the U.S. on holiday for Independence Day.</p>
<p>The market would resume trading on Monday.</p>
<p>On Thursday the long bond closed up 1-3/32 on the day at 100-00 in New York to yield 6.62 percent, after June payrolls came in below expectations, dampening the prospects of an interest rate increase in August.</p>
